s consisting of distribution pipelines, backbone and local transmission pipelines, and various storage facilities. It serves residential, commercial, industrial, and agricultural customers, as well as natural gas-fired electric generation facilities. The company was incorporated in 1995 and is based in Oakland, California.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Patricia Kessler Poppe | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $8.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 29K people. Revenue per employee of $860K ranks in the below the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Pacific Gas & Electric Co. is a large-cap utilities business with a $29.2B market cap on $24.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $3.1B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 12.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 36% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.35559390794755813},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (83% sell ratio, net $3.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Utilities peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Utilities peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Utilities peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 29% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PG&E (PCG) Stock Could Be 38% Stretched Despite Undergrounding Progress","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-pcg/pge/news/pge-pcg-stock-could-be-38-stretched-despite-undergrounding-p","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794569231.939,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.434,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"PG&E (PCG) Approved A Battery Connection Rollout For 35 Million Californians","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/